swallow a missing setter, so one run lists them all

A missing setter raises, the process dies, and the NEXT missing setter is only visible after another
build. Finding four of them on one iA Writer text field cost four builds and about forty minutes.

With CIDER_SWALLOW_SETTERS set, a one argument set... message with no implementation is DROPPED and
named on stderr as SWALLOWED, so a single run lists every one. Pointed at the same application it
answered in one run what four builds had been answering one at a time.

ONLY a setter, and only one taking a single argument, because those return void: the caller reads
nothing back, so dropping the message loses a stored value rather than a computed answer. Anything
else still raises exactly as before.

IT MUST STAY OFF FOR ANY RUN THAT JUDGES WHETHER AN APPLICATION WORKS. An application configured by
messages that went nowhere is not the application, and a capture taken with this on is not evidence
about it.
